lex:tapi-photonic-media-mcg-connectivity-service-end-point-spec
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "mcg-connectivity-service-end-point-spec" ;
    skos:definition "Grouping definition: mcg-connectivity-service-end-point-spec" ;
    skos:scopeNote "MCG provisioning scenarios:\n1) In case of MCG provisioning based on multiple SIPs (e.g. more add/drop ports each one potentially supporting a single OTSi),\nthen a unique/top CSEP instance (not referring to any SIP, with a MC LPC including McgConnectivityServiceEndPointSpec with specified only the number of MCs) refers to\nthe CSEP instances (one per each MEDIA Link, each one referring to one SIP, each one with a MC LPC including McgConnectivityServiceEndPointSpec composing only one MC config pac), through the CSEPHasAssembledCSEPs association.\n2) In case of MCG provisioning based on single SIP, then the model is compacted into only one CSEP instance, with a MC LPC including McgConnectivityServiceEndPointSpec, which composes one or more MC config pacs)." ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:GroupingKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/grouping/tapi-photonic-media/mcg-connectivity-service-end-point-spec> .

